{
  "_about": "Laravel overlay (generic, public). Sources: the Request object and the request() helper. Sinks: raw SQL entry points — DB::raw/select/statement and the *Raw query-builder methods; bound parameters are not sinks (the builder quotes them). Sanitizers: e() = htmlspecialchars. Blade templates ({{ }} escapes, {!! !!} does not) are NOT parsed by php-parser as PHP sinks — a boundary, named here. IDENTIFIER positions are sinks too: the query builder binds VALUES, never column names — orderBy($col), where($col, ...), select($cols), groupBy($col) with request data are injections; only the first argument (the identifier) is judged, bound values are not. Helpers that return configuration, translations, paths or CSRF tokens are TRANSPARENT (taint passes through their arguments; over constants they are constants). old() replays previous REQUEST input: a source.",
